.TH MDB 1
.SH NAME
mdb \- Dis module debugger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdb
.RB [ -w ]
.I file
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mdb
is an adb-style debugger for a compiled Dis
.B .dis
module: it reads
.IR file 's
own header (instructions, strings, types, and other module
attributes) and lets an address-format command language inspect them
\(em an address or expression, an optional count, and a format letter
(.BR x , d , u , o
for hex/decimal/unsigned/octal,
.BR s , r
and their uppercase forms for strings, and more), plus
.B $
commands for module-level summaries (data segment, header, link
table, and so on).
.PP
.B -w
opens
.I file
for writing so some attributes stored in the module's own header can
be changed. If
.I command
is given on the command line it is run once, non-interactively;
otherwise
.I mdb
reads commands from standard input.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/mdb.b
